1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,623
A million bucks, two briefcases left. Stay or switch? Your gut's wrong.

2
00:00:03,873 --> 00:00:06,197
Three cases, one has the cash. You picked one.

3
00:00:06,447 --> 00:00:09,629
The host knows where the cash is, and always opens an empty one.

4
00:00:09,879 --> 00:00:12,001
Tap the heart if you're thinking fifty-fifty.

5
00:00:12,851 --> 00:00:14,976
Nah. Your pick was one in three. Still is.

6
00:00:15,226 --> 00:00:17,172
Send this to the friend who'll argue.

7
00:00:17,422 --> 00:00:20,269
The other— the case he skipped? That one's two in three. Yeah.

8
00:00:21,169 --> 00:00:24,319
Don't buy two in three? Follow, this page settles arguments.

9
00:00:24,719 --> 00:00:28,249
The real game-show host tried it himself. Guess what won? Switching.

10
00:00:28,549 --> 00:00:30,501
So… stay or switch? One word.
